  "solution": {
    "text": "The heating of oxime of acetone in presence of conc. <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> to form N-methyl ethanamide is called Beckmann rearrangement. In Beckmann rearrangement, R-migrates from carbon to nitrogen of an oxime to form N-substituted amide.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0026_ff60f83182f7.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:3.11667in;height:0.825in\" /><br />Loss of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> occurs with simultaneous migration of the trans-R'.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0026_02f352feebc5.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:5.01667in;height:1.03333in\" />"
  }
}